  "limitations": [
    "Plans derive immediate parent directory and unchanged literal query from the empty current search only; next calls are labels.",
    "Fixed recursive no-line-number output is a new search operation, not an equivalent rendering of the failed source command. Exact match means same normalized target operation.",
    "Only plain grep, simple literal patterns and one explicit repository file are supported; regex, pipes, redirects, bundles, multiple paths and root-wide fallback abstain.",
    "A runtime executor must enumerate a symlink-free unchanged parent tree within file/count/byte bounds before a registered grep execution. Those historical filesystem conditions are not verified.",
    "Whole singleton next response and bounded successful/no-match result are required. Removing accompanying reasoning may affect task quality.",
    "Gross token usage belongs to matched original calls, not measured savings. Router, traversal/execution, false-positive, extra-output and future-cache costs are excluded.",
    "Cache and reasoning counts are subsets of input/output totals; no double counting.",
    "Discovery and validation are issue-grouped within an already reused corpus; no untouched external validation claim.",
    "No recorded commands executed or paid inference used."
  ]
